# Secrets. `.env` holds the database URI and the JWT signing key; committing it
# would put both in the repo's history permanently, where rotating them is the
# only remedy. Only the .example files, which carry placeholders, belong in git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

